<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Virius Lupus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 197</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century">2nd century</a> · Also known as Lucius Virius Lupus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lucius Virius Lupus was Roman governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> from about 197, appointed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/septimius-severus">Septimius Severus</a> after the defeat of the usurper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/clodius-albinus">Clodius Albinus</a>. With the province's garrison weakened, he bought peace from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maeatae">Maeatae</a> with large payments, as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cassius-dio">Cassius Dio</a> reports, and he restored forts in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>. His successors prepared the ground for Severus' own campaigns in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> from 208.</p></div>
